          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Most of the earliest instances of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            used in mathematics were for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            indexed by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+set"} partially ordered set
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limit"} sequential
                (co)limits
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codirected+limits"} codirected limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimits"} directed colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
            (much as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            generalise fruitfully to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
            %em filtered (co)limit
            is a further generalisation of this, essentially removing the requirement that the indexing category be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            while preserving the directedness aspect in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            way.
          %p
            Another very important class of early limits and colimits involved situations that generalised
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+subsets"} family of subsets
            of some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            defined on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhoods"} open neighbourhoods
            of some point in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            will have this property. It was noticed that these limits and colimits behaved very nicely and a closer look showed that it was the
            %em (co)filtering
            nature of the indexing category that was the key. This also leads us to filtered (co)limits.
          %p
            So, a
            %em filtered colimit
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            from a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
            %em cofiltered limit
            (sometimes called a filtered limit) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            from a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+category"} cofiltered category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                a colimit being filtered is equivalent to its commuting with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              \-filtered colimit
            is one over a
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            these are precisely the colimits that commute with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+limit"} small limit
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong filtered colimit
              or
              %strong finitely filtered colimit
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D \to C
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                \-filtered colimit
              is one over a
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %p
              Similarly, a
              %strong cofiltered limit
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              of a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D \to C
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+category"} cofiltered category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D \to C
              (that is a functor
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D^{op} \to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is a filtered category.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A cofiltered limit may also be called a
              %strong filtered limit
              (although this can be unclear); the respective terms
              %strong
                filtered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+limit"} direct limit
              and
              %strong
                filtered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+limit"} inverse limit
              are also popular.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            that preserves all finitely filtered colimits is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+functor"} finitary functor
            \.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#filtered_colimits_commute_with_small_limits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            \-Filtered colimits commute with
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            The following is the crucial property of filtered colimits: that they
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+with+colimits"} commute
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              categories and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \,\colon\, C \times D \longrightarrow Set
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\;
                    \\underset{\underset{D}{\longleftarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\underset{D}{\longleftarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\;
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to the limit over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              of the colimit over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              is given by a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi d
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_d
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\;
                    \\underset{\underset{D}{\longleftarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F(-,d)
            %p
              are in turn given by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              with components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\lambda_d)_c
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\underset{\underset{D}{\longleftarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F(c,-)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F(-,d)
                    \\,.
            %p This finally take to have as components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\underset{D}{\longleftarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F(c,d)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    F(c,d)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\underset{C}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                    \\,
                    F(c,d)
                    \\,.
            %p One checks that this indeed implies that all the components are natural and gives the existence of the original morphism.
            %p
              Notice that in general
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              is
              %em not
              an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              We say the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mi D
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\lim_\leftarrow}_D F(-,-)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+with+colimits"} commutes
              with the colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\lim_\to}_C F(-,-)
              if the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              above is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mi D
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mi D
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\lim_\to}_C {\lim_\leftarrow}_D F
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    {\lim_\leftarrow}_D {\lim_\to}_C  F
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
          #FilteredColimitsCommuterWithFiniteLimits.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+with+colimits"} commute
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            %p
              In fact,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+categories"} filtered categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              are precisely those shapes of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              categories such that colimits over them commute with all finite limits in Sets.
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            Proof of the first part is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MacLane71"} MacLane (1971), §IX.2 Thm. 1 (p. 211)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Borceux"} Borceux (1994), theorem I2.13.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BJTS14"} BJTS 14
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+and+colimits+by+example"} limits and colimits by example
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              It is not true that filtered colimits and finite limits commute in
              %em any
              category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              which has them. A simple example is where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces"} closed subspaces
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \{\infty\}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
              ranges over finite subsets of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times colim_i B_i = \{\infty\} \cap (\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}) = \{\infty\}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mi i
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∅
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_i A \times B_i = colim_i \{\infty\} \cap B_i = colim_i \varnothing = \varnothing
          %p
            According to 1.5 and 1.21 in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LPAC"} LPAC
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimits"} directed colimits
            precisely if it has
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-directed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                here
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/directed+colimits+imply+filtered+colimits"} ?
          %p
            The fact that directed colimits suffice to obtain all filtered ones may be regarded as a convenience similar to the fact that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            can be constructed from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            result holds for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codirected+limits"} codirected limits
          %h3#flat_functors_and_points_of_presheaf_toposes Flat functors and points of presheaf toposes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a small category. A functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C \to Set
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat
            if it is a filtered colimit of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
          %p
            Equivalently, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C \to Set
            is flat if and only if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+functors"} tensor product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes_C F: Set^{C^{op}} \to Set
          %p
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is flat if and only if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
            (preserves finite limits). Since this tensor product is automatically a left adjoint, we have the following basic result:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos points
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
              (i.e.,
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to Set^{C^{op}}
              and natural transformations between them) is equivalent to the category of flat modules on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#description_in_set_grp_top_and_alike Description in Set, Grp, Top and alike
          %p
            Elements in filtered colimits in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            are given as classes of equivalences, so called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germs"} germs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            are given as families of compatible elements, so called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/threads"} threads
          %h3#more More
          %p
            (More was/is to be written here, including an application to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"}> filtered category
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sifted+colimit"}> sifted colimit
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sifted+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} sifted (∞,1)-colimit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"}> filtered (∞,1)-colimit
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+homotopy+colimit"} filtered homotopy colimit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kolmogorov+product"} Kolmogorov product
          %p
            Filtered colimits are also important in the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
            categories. See also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-object
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#MacLane71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §IX.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
            %li#Borceux
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 2.13 in:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                  vol 1
            %li
              %p
                Hajnal Andréka and István Németi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Direct limits and filtered colimits are strongly equivalent in all categories
          %p Also
          %ul
            %li#BJTS14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marie+Bjerrum"}> Marie Bjerrum
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
              = succeed "," do
